<title>INDIA: India, South Africa sign treaty on double taxation.</title>
<headline>India, South Africa sign treaty on double taxation.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>India and South Africa on Wednesday signed an agreement to avoid double taxation and boost trade between the two countries, an Indian government statement said.</p>
<p>It said the agreement was signed by Indian Finance Minister P. Chidambaram and South African Trade and Industry Minister Alec Erwin.</p>
<p>&quot;The agreement seeks to provide a fresh impetus to the mutual flow of investment, technology, trade and services between the two countries,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>&quot;The agreement provides for lower rates of taxation in case of dividends, interest, royalties and fees for technical services,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11-301 2024</p>
</text>
